        <mxCell id="header-sub" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-ligatures:none&quot;&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#e2e8f0&quot; style=&quot;font-size:13px&quot;&gt;Which links cross between the on-prem hub and the public clouds, who opens them, and what allows them?&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;Scope: every connection between the K3s hub, the public cloud target (drawn once for EKS cnp-eks and GKE cnp-gke: same links), the buckets, GitHub and the operator · main as of 2026-11-21 · cloud collectors as in Cloud#50 (wave V6, open) · derived from code: K3s/k8s/config/{wireguard,argocd,observability}, K3s/terraform/{roles.tf,policies}, Cloud/terraform/public/{aws/EKS,gcp/GKE}/{cnp.sh,main.tf,kubernetes}, platform/{observability,argo-rollouts}, CMP/backend/app/services/kube_client.py&lt;br&gt;Out of scope: projects, apps and their tunnels to Cloudflare (see multicloud) · tenants of the hub · what observability does with the data (see observability)&lt;br&gt;v0.5 (2026-11-21: Alloy, Loki and the VictoriaMetrics cluster removed, CNP-276) · source: cnp-docs/architecture/cnp&lt;/span&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=JetBrains Mono,Noto Sans Mono,DejaVu Sans Mono,monospace;fontSize=11;fontColor=#94a3b8;" vertex="1" parent="1">
